  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2401.13649",
  "abstract": "VisualWebArena is a benchmark suite designed to assess the performance of multimodal agents on realistic visually grounded web tasks. It comprises 910 tasks across three diverse web environments: Classifieds, Shopping, and Reddit. The tasks require agents to process visual and textual information, interpret natural language instructions, and execute actions on websites to achieve user-defined objectives.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Imagine you're trying to find a specific product on a website. You need to navigate through multiple pages, understand the product's features, and make a purchase. <strong>VisualWebArena</strong> is a benchmark suite that tests the ability of autonomous agents to perform such tasks. It focuses on <strong>visually grounded web tasks</strong>, which require agents to process visual and textual information to achieve user-defined objectives.",
